# Custom IoC rule: DNS queries for domains on abuse.ch URLhaus's known-malicious
# hostname list (https://urlhaus.abuse.ch/downloads/hostfile/). NOT the full URLhaus
# ruleset -- that's ~30k content-heavy HTTP rules, tried twice and OOM-killed this Pi
# both times (see DEPLOYMENT.md, 2026-07-20). This uses Suricata's `dataset` feature
# instead: one lightweight rule doing a hash-set membership test against a flat,
# deduplicated domain list (~350 entries), refreshed by scripts/refresh-ioc-datasets.sh.
#
# `type string` datasets require base64-encoded entries in the loaded file (confirmed
# empirically via `suricata -T` -- plain text fails with "bad base64 encoding"; this
# is not documented consistently and must not be assumed). The dataset file itself is
# generated by refresh-ioc-datasets.sh, not committed to the repo.
#
# Custom sid range 9500000-9599999, clear of et/open (2000000s) and abuse.ch feed sids.
alert dns any any -> any any (msg:"IOC URLhaus known-malicious domain queried"; dns.query; dataset:isset,urlhaus-domains,type string,load /var/lib/suricata/rules.local/urlhaus-domains.dat; classtype:trojan-activity; sid:9500001; rev:1; metadata:created_at 2026_07_26;)
